CI recovery and validation sharding

Observed and fixed:
- CI resolved OpenSSL through the pinned SDK pkg-config wrapper; OpenSSL now uses the system pkg-config while PipeWire remains pinned.
- CI installs the Wasm Rust target, uses current mise formatting, and has deterministic admission/corpus tests.
- Overlay tests have a hermetic Mesa/Wayland runtime and bounded browser startup.
- The prior sequential CI run took 23m41s.

Parallelization:
- Split mise run test and the CI matrix into checks, capture, runtime, overlay-native, overlay-browser, overlay-embedded-unit, and overlay-embedded-integration.
- Every CI shard was verified from a checkout with no target directory and produces its own required artifacts.
- The local aggregate prebuilds shared skin and web outputs before launching the same seven shards in parallel, avoiding concurrent writes to shared target artifacts.
- Browser and software Vulkan packages are installed only for the shards that need them.

